# Update origins this BlackBox accepts, one URL per line (# starts a comment).
#
# Scripts/install.sh publishes this file, root-owned, as
# /etc/blackbox/update-origin (publish_update_pins). Scripts/update.sh and the
# in-app updater (Orchestrator/update/verify.py) fetch updates only while the
# checkout's `git remote get-url origin` is one of these URLs, compared
# ignoring case, one trailing "/" and one trailing ".git".
#
# The pin comes from this tracked file, never from the box's .git/config, which
# the running service can write. A fork that ships its own updates lists its
# own URL here. A box that must fetch from somewhere else (a mirror) adds that
# URL to /etc/blackbox/update-origin as root; install.sh rewrites the file from
# this one, so the line has to be added again after each install.sh run.
